# The SMB world select: `task build-cd-iff-smb-menu` packs these levels, in this order, behind
# wfsource/source/game/shell-menu.fth, and writes the title, prompt and names into the bundle's
# MENU chunk (wflevels/smb-menu-cd.iff). Same levels and TOC order as `task build-cd-iff-smb`
# (wflevels/smb-cd.iff), so the flag/axe ActBoxes (LEVEL_TO_RUN = 1, 2, 3, 0) still chain
# W1-1 -> W1-2 -> W1-3 -> W1-4 -> W1-1 from whichever world the player starts in.
# Format: `title <text>`, `prompt <text>`, then `level <path> | <name>`; paths relative to this
# file; text is printable ASCII, 1 to 60 characters. The names are placeholders (the project
# does not own the "Super Mario Bros." name); the user picks the real ones.
# Plan: docs/plans/2026-10-01-level-menu-selector.md
title WF SMB
prompt Choose a world
level smb_w1_1-standalone.iff | World 1-1
level smb_w1_2-standalone.iff | World 1-2
level smb_w1_3-standalone.iff | World 1-3
level smb_w1_4-standalone.iff | World 1-4
